WEBVTT

00:27:57.770 --> 00:28:00.837
because if you think about it,

00:28:00.861 --> 00:28:02.926
the currency of getting
to know someone well

00:28:02.950 --> 00:28:05.013
is that you're sharing
information with them

00:28:05.037 --> 00:28:07.711
that you might not share
with everybody else around you.

00:28:07.735 --> 00:28:09.932
But if everybody's hearing
everything you say,

00:28:09.956 --> 00:28:13.664
there's not as much of an opportunity
to develop those connections.

00:28:13.688 --> 00:28:17.102
So, the data was all there.

00:28:17.126 --> 00:28:18.930
Yeah, and I started talking about it,

00:28:18.954 --> 00:28:24.078
and boy, did that
touch a nerve with people.

00:28:24.102 --> 00:28:27.593
CA: Indeed! Well, it touched
a nerve with me, for one thing.

00:28:27.617 --> 00:28:29.641
When you said that in your talk,

00:28:29.665 --> 00:28:35.418
like, ideas spark when you have this sort
of catalyst of a creative person here